window.docContents[113].resolve({"/#A-Property-Kind-Calculus-for-Metrology___-proving-quantity-and-unit-laws-in-Lean___-from-ISO___IEC-80000-to-measurement-uncertainty--Onboarding___-Human-Context-Protocols--L1-___-Two-bodies--Persona":{"contents":"You are a PhysLib contributor: a physicist who writes Lean in PhysLib. You know Lean and\nPhysLib and trust Dimension and WithDim; L0 has already shown what those dimensions\ncan and cannot distinguish.\n\n","context":"A Property Kind Calculus for Metrology: proving quantity and unit laws in Lean, from ISO/IEC 80000 to measurement uncertainty\u0009Onboarding: Human Context Protocols\u0009L1 — Two bodies","header":"5.2.2. Persona","id":"/#A-Property-Kind-Calculus-for-Metrology___-proving-quantity-and-unit-laws-in-Lean___-from-ISO___IEC-80000-to-measurement-uncertainty--Onboarding___-Human-Context-Protocols--L1-___-Two-bodies--Persona"},"/#A-Property-Kind-Calculus-for-Metrology___-proving-quantity-and-unit-laws-in-Lean___-from-ISO___IEC-80000-to-measurement-uncertainty--Onboarding___-Human-Context-Protocols--L4-___-Out-of-the-line--Synopsis--Verifiable-properties":{"contents":"* Adding a position to a displacement fails to type-check, and so does adding a distance to the length of a displacement: there is no HAdd instance for either pair of kinds (refused) HCP.L4_OutOfTheLine#points_vectors_and_distances.* Pair P's A–B separation is an IndividualQuantity of kind distance about P, and pair Q's separation supplied where P's is expected fails with a type mismatch (refused) HCP.L4_OutOfTheLine#whose_distance.* The distance between two points equals the length of the displacement between them (theorem) HCP.L4_OutOfTheLine#distance_is_length.* kBoostTransport rejects a displacement with a type mismatch, and adding a velocity to a force fails to type-check (refused) HCP.L4_OutOfTheLine#kinded_frames.* Converting P's displacement from frame F to frame G with kGeometricTransport gives the displacement that G computes from its own coordinates (theorem) HCP.L4_OutOfTheLine#kinded_frames.* The displacement of the cart's origin between times t₁ and t₂ equals the elapsed time times the cart's velocity (theorem) HCP.L4_OutOfTheLine#observer_motion.\n\n","context":"A Property Kind Calculus for Metrology: proving quantity and unit laws in Lean, from ISO/IEC 80000 to measurement uncertainty\u0009Onboarding: Human Context Protocols\u0009L4 — Out of the line\u0009Synopsis","header":"5.5.1.3. Verifiable properties","id":"/#A-Property-Kind-Calculus-for-Metrology___-proving-quantity-and-unit-laws-in-Lean___-from-ISO___IEC-80000-to-measurement-uncertainty--Onboarding___-Human-Context-Protocols--L4-___-Out-of-the-line--Synopsis--Verifiable-properties"}});